    "Id": "chassisdef_supernova_SNV-SUPRA",
    "Name": "Supernova",
    "Details": "The Supranova began as the personal experiment of a Society scientist who considered the venerable Supernova less a BattleMech than an unanswered question: just how far could its six-laser concept be pushed? The answer was six Large Supra Lasers—and an increasingly unhinged effort to keep them from melting the machine around them. Making the concept remotely practical required an extravagant thermal-management system incorporating rare Proto Heat Sinks and additional experimental cooling equipment, allowing the Supranova to sustain a volume of energy fire that would cripple lesser designs. A Nova CEWS suite was added to provide the targeting and electronic warfare capabilities expected of modern Society machines. Whether the resulting BattleMech represents a triumph of Society engineering or merely proof that its creator should have been more closely supervised remains a matter of debate.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Combat Computer</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.2</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Left Lower, Right Lower</color>",
